---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqSchema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What happens to my current hosting?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your site moves to my infrastructure. Once everything's verified and running, you cancel your old hosting. I handle the full migration. DNS, files, database, email routing. Zero downtime."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I still have access to my site?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Absolutely. You keep full WordPress admin access. Log in, edit content, publish posts, whatever you need. I handle the infrastructure and the stuff that requires technical knowledge."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What if I want to leave?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It's month-to-month after onboarding. No lock-in. If you leave, I'll give you a full backup and 30 days to migrate elsewhere. Your site is always yours."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What about my domain and email?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Your domain stays yours. I never take ownership. Email routing is preserved during migration. If you're on shared hosting email, I'll help you set up something proper that won't break when the hosting changes."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do maintenance hours roll over?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "They don't. Hours are use-it-or-lose-it each month. Keeps pricing predictable for both of us. If you consistently need more, we'll adjust your tier. Consistently need fewer, same thing."
      }
    }
  ]
});
---

<Base title="Web Management | Managed WordPress Hosting & Security" description="Managed WordPress hosting, security, updates, and monthly reporting. Your site lives on my infrastructure.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqSchema} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Services","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Web Management","item":"https://codyasmith.com/services/web-management"}]})} />
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative pt-40 pb-24 px-6 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[600px] h-[400px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/services" class="reveal inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-500 text-sm hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors duration-300 mb-8 group">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 16l-4-4m0 0l4-4m-4 4h18" />
        </svg>
        All services
      </a>
      <h1 class="reveal font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl text-neutral-100 leading-[1.05] mb-10">
        Web Management
      </h1>
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed">
        I ask clients who hosts their website. Most of them don't know. They think it's GoDaddy but they're not sure. Nobody's logged in since the last developer left. The SSL certificate expired two months ago and nobody noticed until a customer mentioned the warning screen. That's the moment I usually get the call.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What happens -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="reveal font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-neutral-100 mb-12">Here's how it works.</h2>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">First, I move everything.</h3>
          <p>
            DNS, hosting, email routing, plugins, database. Your site comes off whatever shared box it's been sitting on and onto dedicated cloud infrastructure under my management. Zero downtime. You don't touch anything. You don't even notice it happened, except the site gets faster.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">Then I take the thing apart.</h3>
          <p>
            Plugin conflicts, outdated dependencies, security holes, performance problems nobody told you about. Everything gets documented. This becomes your first Site Health Report and the baseline for everything that comes after.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">After that, it becomes invisible to you.</h3>
          <p>
            Updates get tested before they touch your live site. Security monitoring runs around the clock. Backups happen daily. And when something breaks, because eventually something always does, my phone buzzes. Not yours.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-xl font-medium mb-3">First of every month, a report lands in your inbox.</h3>
          <p>
            Plain language. What I did, what I found, what's coming next, and how performance compares to last month. You never have to wonder if the money's doing anything. The report is the receipt.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What's covered -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="reveal font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-neutral-100 mb-8">What's covered.</h2>
      <div class="reveal text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
        <p>Dedicated cloud hosting. Not shared with hundreds of other sites. Fast, isolated, and fully under my control.</p>
        <p>SSL certificates, firewall configuration, malware scanning, and login hardening. Problems caught before you know they exist.</p>
        <p>WordPress core, theme, and plugin updates, tested in staging before going live. No "update all and hope" approach.</p>
        <p>Automated daily backups with point-in-time restoration. If something goes wrong, we roll back in minutes.</p>
        <p>Uptime monitoring every 60 seconds. If your site goes down, I know about it before your customers do.</p>
        <p>And the monthly Site Health Report tying it all together.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tiers -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6 surface-1">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-neutral-100 mb-4">Three tiers. Pick the one that fits.</h2>
        <p class="text-neutral-400">Priced by site complexity. Pages, integrations, and traffic. Month-to-month after onboarding. Multi-site discounts available.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 reveal-stagger" id="tier-cards">
        <!-- Good -->
        <div class="reveal glow-card tier-card p-8 flex flex-col hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-300" style="--i:0">
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-2">Good</p>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-2xl font-medium mb-1">Essentials</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-6">Your site stays up, stays secure, stays updated. The basics, handled.</p>
          <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm space-y-3 mb-4 flex-1">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Managed cloud hosting
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Security & SSL
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Core & plugin updates
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Daily backups
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Uptime monitoring
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Monthly Site Health Report
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-neutral-600 text-xs mb-6 italic">Does not include content changes, performance optimization, or dedicated support hours.</p>
          <a href="/contact?interest=web-management" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 border border-white/10 text-neutral-300 font-medium text-sm rounded-lg hover:border-white/25 hover:text-neutral-100 transition-all duration-300">
            Get started
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Better -->
        <div class="reveal glow-card tier-card p-8 flex flex-col ring-1 ring-amber-500/30 relative md:scale-[1.03] hover:scale-[1.05] transition-transform duration-300" style="--i:1">
          <div class="absolute -top-3 left-8 px-3 py-1 bg-amber-500 text-neutral-950 text-xs font-semibold rounded-full">
            Where most clients land
          </div>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-2">Better</p>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-2xl font-medium mb-1">Professional</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-6">For businesses that depend on their site to generate leads.</p>
          <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm space-y-3 mb-8 flex-1">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Everything in Essentials
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              More included hours
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Quarterly performance reporting
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Content updates & minor edits
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Performance optimization
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/contact?interest=web-management" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 bg-amber-500 text-neutral-950 font-semibold text-sm rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-400 transition-all duration-300 hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(245,158,11,0.25)]">
            Get started
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Best -->
        <div class="reveal glow-card tier-card p-8 flex flex-col hover:scale-[1.02] transition-transform duration-300" style="--i:2">
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs tracking-[0.15em] uppercase mb-2">Best</p>
          <h3 class="text-neutral-100 text-2xl font-medium mb-1">Priority</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-6">For sites where downtime costs real money and fast response isn't optional.</p>
          <ul class="text-neutral-400 text-sm space-y-3 mb-8 flex-1">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Everything in Professional
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Same-day priority response
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Maximum included hours
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Training included
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-amber-400 mt-0.5">&#10003;</span>
              Dedicated monthly call
            </li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/contact?interest=web-management" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 border border-white/10 text-neutral-300 font-medium text-sm rounded-lg hover:border-white/25 hover:text-neutral-100 transition-all duration-300">
            Get started
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="reveal mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-neutral-100">Questions I get asked.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4 reveal-stagger">
        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:0">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What happens to my current hosting?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            It moves to mine. I handle DNS, files, database, email routing. Once everything's running and you've confirmed it, you cancel the old account. Zero downtime. Most clients don't even realize the switch happened until they see the speed difference.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:1">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            Do I still have access to my site?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Yes. Full WordPress admin. Log in, edit content, publish posts. It's your site. I handle the engine room. You keep the keys to the front door.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:2">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What if I want to leave?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Month-to-month after onboarding. No contracts, no lock-in. If you leave, I hand you a full backup and give you 30 days to land somewhere else. I don't hold sites hostage. That's the other guy's move.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:3">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            What about my domain and email?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            Your domain is yours. I never touch ownership. Email keeps working through the migration. If you're currently running email through your shared host (and a lot of people are without realizing it), I'll set up something that won't go dark when the old hosting gets canceled.
          </div>
        </details>

        <details class="reveal group glow-card" style="--i:4">
          <summary class="p-6 cursor-pointer flex items-center justify-between text-neutral-100 font-medium">
            Do maintenance hours roll over?
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-neutral-500 group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 4v16m8-8H4" /></svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-6 text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            No. Use them or lose them. Keeps it simple and keeps pricing honest for both of us. If you're consistently using more than your tier allows, we bump you up. Consistently using fewer, we bump you down. Nobody pays for time they're not using.
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="relative py-32 px-6 surface-1 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[500px] h-[300px] bg-amber-500/5 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
      <p class="reveal text-neutral-400 text-lg mb-10">Tell me what you're running and I'll tell you what the migration looks like.</p>
      <a href="/contact?interest=web-management" class="reveal inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 bg-amber-500 text-neutral-950 font-semibold text-sm rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-400 transition-all duration-300 hover:shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(245,158,11,0.25)]">
        Let's talk
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
